+importance.
 
-Feature fusion F3 combines a 128-dimensional visual projection with the 220 statistical numerical features through separate projections, normalization and a fitted classifier. Its recorded candidates use hidden widths 32 or 64 and ten or twenty epochs. Context gates instead allocate weights over branch logits. Their candidates have hidden width eight or sixteen and forty epochs. Action-only, quality-only and combined contexts remain different models, as do a static gate with context held constant and a gate exposed to corrupted OOF records.\ev{Fusion and gate configurations}{\EvidenceRef{E054}{}}
