 \subsection{Interpretation and Limitations}
-The retained learned predictors do not establish an improvement over the constant under this task and protocol. That conclusion is narrower than ``the sensors have no damage information.'' The target may not align with the physical signal, a model can be underfit or overfit, and cross-experiment acquisition differences may dominate the small training population. Twenty nominal runs also do not eliminate dependence caused by repeated or equal derived sequences.
-
-Run-cluster intervals describe resampling of saved outcomes conditional on fitted models. They do not quantify full training-seed variation or uncertainty over a population of independent test machines. With only three experiments, the number of genuinely different deployment domains remains small. The unresolved target meaning, the profile's loss of tooth identity and padding/provenance concerns additionally limit interpretation. These qualifications do not erase a negative comparison; they identify which hypothesis it actually challenges.\ev{PHM comparison and target validity}{\EvidenceRef{E106}{}}
