-\section{Architecture Reuse and Dataset-Specific Adaptations}
-The pretrained condition (P) used the ResNet18-vd CNN backbone inside the RT-DETR-R18vd checkpoint \citep{Zhao2024RTDETR}. The extractor stopped at the CNN feature maps, before the hybrid Transformer encoder, detection decoder, and box heads. Spatial means from the last three maps yielded 896 features per frame. Averaging across sixteen frames gave one vector per cutting interval. With the backbone frozen, a newly fitted $896\rightarrow128\rightarrow1$ head with ReLU and dropout~0.1 supplied the target prediction. It had 114,945 trainable parameters.
-
-The numerical branch is a fresh balanced L2 logistic regression on the ninety statistics, with $C=1$. A separately fitted histogram gradient boosting model provides the stronger sensor control. It is essential to keep that control separate: F2 consumes the logistic branch, not the HGB predictions. Averaging combines the two branch probabilities without a fitted fusion parameter. Original F2 is a newly fitted unweighted L2 logistic model on visual and sensor probabilities generated out of fold. No source failure head, scaler, calibrator or fusion coefficient is transferred.\ev{MSM executed composition}{\EvidenceRef{E077}{}}
-
-The clean and augmented quality gates are additional comparisons. They reuse a small softmax gate over branch logits, with label-free image-quality summaries, numerical variability, missing-channel fractions and availability flags. These summaries may encode process context as well as degradation. A changing allocation therefore is not a calibrated estimate of modality reliability. This matters because a reliability-aware fusion argument requires a quality proxy that actually predicts error, rather than a proxy that merely changes with the input \citep{Zhang2023QMF}. QG-clean uses clean OOF views. QG-aug sees clean views plus seven predefined lowest-severity corruptions, while F2-aug is the exposure-matched static control. Clean fitting, corruption exposure and quality conditioning remain separate interventions.
-
-R denotes a different question: initialization from a specifically completed REASSEMBLE-learned CNN. The exact canonical source required by MSM's gate was unavailable in the inspected evaluation, so that condition remains unmeasured. This does not contradict the P completion or the later, differently specified ViFailback donor study. Architecture reuse, generic pretraining and transfer of task-learned weights retain separate provenance.
-
-\section{Implementation Checks and Bounded Development Runs}
-The bounded development exercise was an engineering check: its two-epoch, at-most-24-interval design restricted head updates and CNN frame forwards and prohibited outer-assessment predictions. It could expose shape, gradient, memory or reload errors, but could not estimate generalization. Generalization was assessed in the subsequent evaluation on held-out intervals.
-
-The saved implementation audit checks planned cases, source identities, native assessment units, model budgets and checkpoint reloads. It also refits the fixed F2 estimator from saved clean OOF probabilities and reports zero coefficient discrepancy. The CNN cache check reports maximum difference zero on an outer-training-only example. These support consistency of the saved procedure and its outputs. Their scope is narrower than reproduction of stochastic training: exact reload and metric recomputation cannot alone certify that every training step would recur in another environment.\ev{MSM implementation and reproduction scope}{\EvidenceRef{E078}{}}
-
-\section{Evaluation Protocol and Conditions Without Estimates}
-The completed matrix uses three outer and two inner StratifiedGroupKFold partitions, fixed split seeds and training seeds 42, 123 and 20261023. Inner fits produce branch OOF probabilities for learned fusion; outer assessments remain excluded from fitting. The six target/grouping protocols yield 54 completed case records. The 54 cases include different folds and seeds from overlapping protocols.
-
-The main visual head runs for ten fixed epochs and the gate for forty. The assessment uses a fixed threshold of 0.5, with no assessment-selected epoch or fitted primary calibrator. Scikit-learn computes average precision as a weighted mean of precision values, with each weight equal to the increase in recall \citep{Pedregosa2011ScikitLearn}. This differs from trapezoidal integration of the precision--recall curve. F2 denotes the fusion model in this study. Primary results pool the disjoint outer predictions separately for each seed, then summarize the three APs. An arithmetic mean of fold APs answers a different question because fold prevalences and cross-fold score scales differ.
-
-Conditions with a missing source checkpoint, inadequate class support or insufficient temporal coverage yielded no estimate. The results below cover the conditions that met the original criteria.\ev{MSM fixed evaluation protocol}{\EvidenceRef{E070}{}}
-
