+between assembly and milling. ViFailback gave a similar direction for a different
+endpoint. Original stacking attained pooled macro-AP of .621--.629 across three seeds
+versus .649 for logistic sensing (Table~\ref{tab:vif-bothclass} and Chapter~8). Macro-AP
+here weights success and failure equally. In HANDOVER, averaging the two branch
+predictions gave mean failure AP of .803 on 151 official test trials, below the sensor
+component at .824. The missing participant-to-trial mapping prevented construction of
+the participant-disjoint predictions required to fit the planned stacker. HANDOVER
+therefore supplies a measured comparison for averaging and an open question for learned
+fusion. Across these tasks, the clearest gain occurred for simple prediction fusion in
+assembly. The two other stacking studies and the handover averaging study each favored
+their constituent sensor model on the primary ranking metric.
 
