 \midrule\endhead
-P001 \citep{P001} & Context & Single infrared image restoration; no independently acquired second modality. This is context rather than evidence for a fusion advantage. \\
-P002 \citep{P002} & Context & Infrared machinery diagnosis. Combining thermal regions remains image-only; vibration fusion is proposed as future work. \\
-P003 \citep{P003} & Industrial & Physical camera and audio welding classification. Split independence and controlled missing/noise evaluation are not established in the inspected postprint. \\
-P004 \citep{P004} & Methods & Seminal evaluation foundation on model-selection bias. It does not supply an industrial fusion experiment. \\
-P005 \citep{P005} & Methods & Transferable modality-dropout method. Training exposure and planned available-input configurations determine the robustness claim. \\
-P006 \citep{P006} & Methods & Transferable gated intermediate fusion. Learned allocation alone does not establish calibrated modality reliability. \\
-P007 \citep{P007} & Methods & Transferable robust multimodal classification architecture. The inspected preprint and published journal metadata refer to one work. \\
-P008 \citep{P008} & Methods & Predictive uncertainty under dataset shift. Good in-distribution confidence does not guarantee shifted reliability. \\
-P009 \citep{P009} & Methods & Reproducibility and reporting foundation. Documentation and code availability are distinct from independently reproduced results. \\
-P010 \citep{P010} & Methods & The visual patch Transformer was evaluated on image recognition. The study provides no comparison of the industrial visual models evaluated here. \\
-P011 \citep{P011} & Methods & The audio-spectrogram Transformer represents sound through spectrogram patches. The present studies include no completed audio-branch comparison. \\
-P012 \citep{P012} & Methods & Self-supervised dilated-convolution time-series encoder. It is not a Transformer; the reported Transformer substitution performs worse. \\
-P013 \citep{P013} & Methods & The video Transformer models interactions across space and time. The REASSEMBLE visual classifier averages frame descriptors over time. \\
-P014 \citep{Nagrani2021MBT} & Methods & Audiovisual attention-bottleneck fusion. Transferable representation design does not establish industrial sensor-failure robustness. \\
-P015 \citep{P015} & Methods & Multimodal benchmark and evaluation framework. Its different tasks are not independent replications of one industrial target. \\
-P016 \citep{P016} & Methods & The missing-modality Transformer evaluation includes adverse multimodal results. For the Food dataset, the prose and tabulated unimodal result disagree. \\
-P017 \citep{P017} & Methods & The preprint and published article on leakage in scientific evaluation give different counts of affected papers. \\
-P018 \citep{P018} & Methods & The study evaluates pretrained time-series representations on benchmarks. Transfer of its weights to the industrial tasks considered here was not tested. \\
-P019 \citep{Sliwowski2025REASSEMBLE} & Dataset & The robotic assembly dataset provides native action outcomes. Its published demonstration count differs from the eligible sample for the present action-level analysis. \\
-P020 \citep{P020} & Methods & Transferable multimodal negative-learning study. Its noise regimes and negative comparisons remain specific to the reported tasks. \\
-P021 \citep{P021} & Industrial & Physical tool images and force measurements with adaptive fusion. Post-pass image timing and incompletely reported splits limit prognostic claims. \\
-P022 \citep{P022} & Methods & Non-industrial dynamic-fusion method. Its evidence informs fusion assumptions without constituting industrial deployment validation. \\
-P023 \citep{P023} & Methods & Transferable constrained fusion of text with time series. It supplies negative evidence against assuming every additional modality helps. \\
-P024 \citep{P024} & Industrial & Industrial inspection using geometric prior information. RGB and geometry are distinguished from independent machine telemetry. \\
-P025 \citep{P025} & Industrial & The industrial inspection model combines visual and geometric features with language for defect reporting. Its evaluation includes task-specific supervision and measures report consistency. \\
-P026 \citep{P026} & Industrial & Train-calibrated RGB/geometry fusion includes explicit missing-3D evaluation and static/gated controls. It is not camera-plus-machine-telemetry evidence. \\
-P027 \citep{P027} & Industrial & Audio, vibration and current fusion with missing-input claims. Limited auditability excludes it from strong quantitative synthesis. \\
-P028 \citep{Thoduka2024Handover} & Dataset & Completed robotic handover outcomes with video, force/torque and gripper inputs. Added gripper input reduces one five-class accuracy result. \\
-P029 \citep{Huo2022Multisensor} & Industrial & Thermal-image and vibration fault diagnosis with single-input and noise controls. Reliability conclusions remain conditional on its protocol. \\
-P030 \citep{Nie2023PatchTST} & Methods & PatchTST was evaluated for time-series forecasting. The PHM regression and REASSEMBLE classification experiments trained separate temporal models from scratch. \\
-P031 \citep{P031} & Industrial & Vision-language surface localization is evaluated with pixel metrics. These measure localization rather than image-level detection or numerical process sensing. \\
-P032 \citep{Hua2026Weld} & Industrial & Camera/audio weld-penetration attention fusion. Clean single-input and fused models all report 100\% accuracy; independent-run splitting is unclear. \\
-P033 \citep{P033} & Industrial & RGB/geometry disagreement scoring. Eyecandies image AUROC decreases despite improved localization, showing metric-specific trade-offs. \\
-P034 \citep{P034} & Methods & Space-time attention models cross-frame interactions. The core REASSEMBLE visual representation averages frame descriptors. \\
-P035 \citep{P035} & Context & Weakly supervised single-camera surface inspection. Internal feature fusion is not fusion of independently acquired physical modalities. \\
-P036 \citep{P036} & Methods & Transferable counterargument on attention interpretation. Model inspection does not by itself establish a physical causal explanation. \\
-P037 \citep{Altinses2023Fuzzy} & Simulation & Camera/robot telemetry corruption in simulated pose regression. Overlapping temporal windows and random splitting limit physical-deployment inference. \\
-P038 \citep{P038} & Industrial & RGB/geometry consistency fusion. Its learned scalar mixing coefficient does not demonstrate sample-conditioned online reliability adaptation. \\
-P040 \citep{Bengio2004CVVariance} & Methods & Cross-validation variance theory. Overlapping training folds do not supply independent replications for a naive standard error. \\
-P041 \citep{Guo2017Calibration} & Methods & Validation-fitted calibration foundation. In-distribution temperature scaling is not a guarantee of reliable probabilities after shift. \\
-P042 \citep{P042} & Context & Single-vibration diagnosis with synthetic noise. Simulated target training and reporting inconsistencies limit transfer and field-validity claims. \\
-P043 \citep{P043} & Methods & Distribution-shift benchmark. OOD validation access is explicit; this is not an untouched-target industrial multimodal experiment. \\
-P044 \citep{P044} & Methods & Transferable medical fusion counterexample. Selection and evaluation share validation data; no independent final test is established. \\
-P045 \citep{P045} & Industrial & Post-pass tool photographs and acoustic emission predict wear. Strong visual and adverse multimodal comparators coexist with unresolved tool-split coverage. \\
-P046 \citep{P046} & Industrial & Microphone/accelerometer bearing fusion. Test-noise results lack an equivalent static corruption comparator; recording-disjoint splitting is unclear. \\
-P048 \citep{P048} & Industrial & Thermal-camera and vibration feature fusion. Overlapping windows, multirate pairing and separately fitted speeds restrict generalization claims. \\
-P049 \citep{P049} & Methods & Transferable attention-interpretability critique. Attention perturbation is distinct from physical input corruption or modality dropout. \\
-P050 \citep{P050} & Methods & Transferable unaligned language/audio/video cross-attention. Unequal feature rates are not a controlled hardware-clock offset test. \\
-P051 \citep{P051} & Industrial & Visible/infrared federated detection. Incomplete clients differ from surprise inference outage; group splits, clipped results and coefficient conflicts limit appraisal. \\
-P052 \citep{Kim2026MSM} & Dataset & Milling dataset with laboratory video and machine measurements. Dataset availability enables research but is not itself a learned fusion result. \\
-P053 \citep{P053} & Industrial & Audio/vibration wavelet-image cross-attention. These are transformed signals, not camera images; controlled missing/noise tests are not established. \\
-P054 \citep{P054} & Industrial & RGB/surface-normal anomaly detection. Training feature-noise regularization is distinct from a test-input degradation benchmark. \\
-P055 \citep{P055} & Methods & Proper-scoring-rule foundation. Expected propriety does not certify finite-sample calibration or shifted sensor reliability. \\
-P056 \citep{P056} & Industrial & RGB/point-cloud local alignment preprint, version 1. Checkpoint-selection population and retraining variability remain unclear. \\
-P057 \citep{Zeng2026ViFailback} & Dataset & The study uses visual symbols and language to diagnose manipulation failures. The present ViFailback experiment instead combines camera views and numerical robot observations. \\
-P058 \citep{Zhang2023QMF} & Methods & Transferable quality-aware weighting. Its conditional generalization-upper-bound comparison does not imply universal actual-risk superiority. \\
-P059 \citep{Zhao2024RTDETR} & Methods & Single-image object detector foundation. Executing an extracted CNN backbone does not execute the full detector or its reported inference pipeline. \\
