-\noindent\textit{Data:} CAM-S denotes a physical camera and a separate non-image signal; RGB-G denotes RGB and geometry; OPT-AUD denotes photodiode and acoustic signals, without a camera input. MS denotes machine/process channels; SV denotes parallel representations of the same telemetry; IMG-U has incompletely documented image provenance. SIM-CS/SIM-G are synthetic. RGB, AUD and VIB are single physical modalities; MULTI-CAM uses several imaging sources; X is transferable non-industrial evidence.
-\par\noindent\textit{Fusion:} E, early; I, intermediate; L, output-score fusion; H, hybrid feature/output fusion; KD, privileged cross-modal training; U, unimodal; TAX, taxonomy. Authors' terminology is normalized by where information is combined.
-\par\noindent\textit{Baseline:} M, input variants evaluated within one protocol; P, partial/ambiguous; R, retained-input student with/without teachers; L, literature comparison; A, module/map/task ablations only; U, unimodal reference; S, survey; N, not established. M does not guarantee matched capacity, pretraining or tuning.
